+// OpenWar3 fix: fengari reads `process.env` here BEFORE its own "am I in Node?" guard
+// thirty lines below, so merely importing it in a browser throws "process is not defined".
+// Guarded rather than shimmed: defining a global `process` would flip lbaselib, lauxlib and
+// loadlib onto their NODE paths (they each test `typeof process === "undefined"` to choose),
+// and they would then reach for `process.stdout`. The browser is the platform this engine
+// runs on; fengari's own browser build (fengari-web) makes the same two corrections.
+const conf = (typeof process !== "undefined" && process.env && process.env.FENGARICONF
+    ? JSON.parse(process.env.FENGARICONF) : {});
 
